text=f'''# D04 starboard-aft receiving and court routes

Two enclosed perimeter branches now serve nine broad starboard-aft courts through full-size private staff fittings, controlled by two normal receiving-street staff portals. The 0.75m outer court stays sealed without entry/work-reach acceptance. Existing receiving, commons and lower staff approaches remain shared; full clean/used segregation remains unfinished. Port-aft is the next missing court/receiving package; its wider north platform requires a different source-fit connection design.

The package adds {p['new_floor_m2']:.2f}m² of missing floor with zero duplicate public/commons walking area. All floor framing stays above Y16.26, above the protected D03 Uniforms & Lockers occupied top Y16.25. No lower columns or ceiling cuts are added. There are 108 exact court-floor side joints and 40 exact end-floor joints; source-floor capacity, steel sizing and cantilever engineering remain held.

Essential checks pass: {g['checks']:,} geometry checks, {g['exact_retained_original_meshes']:,} exact affected/protected original meshes, {g['runtime_exact_preimages']} exact runtime preimages, {g['actual_original_controller_gate_pose_samples']} original-controller poses and {g['worker_capsule_samples']} worker capsules. The programme audit passes {vol['conservative_part_programme_volume_checks']:,} checks across 161 programmes without conflicts. Connection passes {conn['checks']} checks and {len(conn['original_player_controller_legs'])} actual-player walking legs, using one original receiving fixture and no route teleports. Normal RMB/E controls operate all thresholds with temporary known private visits; every new gate ends closed with visits cleared. No production permission/provider is invented.

All {len(p['source_protected_native_exports']):,} previous managed native/export files remain byte-identical. Two editable native revisions have byte-identical fresh repeat exports. The 55 fitting copies and ten rigid planter/soil/foliage meshes preserve exact local geometry, UVs, packed texture bytes, roughness and links. Twenty bounded cut successors preserve 98 outside triangles and original UVs. Inactive geometry was independently retained at `{p['independently_retained_inactive_geometry_commit']}` before the exact one-line integration.

Three 64-sample Blender source views show the receiving threshold, short-court threshold and cross passage with original homes/commons/floors/roofs. Diagnostic fill and partial neighborhood context remain explicit; these are not Godot, full-ship, CRT or target-hardware screenshots and do not approve final visuals. The denoising failure and earlier source images remain retained. Library photo delivery failed before bytes with a hosted-app network error; the parent delivered earlier progress images separately.

Original room IDs, 120 allocations/150 reserved rests, public routes, previous staff packages, D05 datums and the approved port-central commons remain intact. Habitat/biology, consent/vacancy/provider, stock/refill/save/inventory/operational returns, loaded-cart vertical, engineering and final visuals remain unfinished. Both earlier narrow starboard-forward/central courts also stay sealed; two historical unpublished native byte versions remain unavailable. All eight construction groups remain unfinished; see FULL_SHIP_SCOPE_INDEX.md for their full obligations. Manual independently verified checkpoints continue with no watcher/credential/network changes.
'''
